<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The adaptive launcher icon for the **neon_mesh** style — the neon glass mark with the shield and the mesh behind it.

  Not a recolour of the mark. The eight colour variants are one artwork with
  its hue shifted; these four are their own pictures, imported by
  scripts/import_icon_styles.py and only resized. See docs/app-icon.md.

  The launcher masks this to whatever shape the device uses, and only the
  middle 72dp of the 108dp canvas is ever visible, so the foreground carries
  the artwork scaled into that window. The background is the same flat black
  the other icons use, which is what the artwork's own black edges disappear
  into under any mask shape.

  **No monochrome layer, on purpose.** A themed icon is drawn as a single
  tone from its alpha, and these pictures are a camouflage pattern, a metal
  plate and a glow — flattening one to a silhouette would produce a filled
  blob with none of what makes it recognisable. A launcher in themed mode
  falls back to the ordinary icon instead, which is the better of the two.
-->
<adaptive-icon xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <background android:drawable="@color/ic_launcher_background" />
    <foreground android:drawable="@mipmap/ic_launcher_neon_mesh_foreground" />
</adaptive-icon>
